      "content": "i mean, i get the political stuff, but is it really that big of a difference in the actual day-to-day operations? like, when we talk about \"professionalism\" or \"reliability,\" are we talking about actual work ethic and how people handle contracts, or is it just the macro stuff? i've heard some people say that doing business in certain regions just requires a different kind of approach because of how people there operate. do you see a pattern in the actual behavior of suppliers in these areas?",
